# PAM stack for pi-panel-compositor.service (PAMName=pi-panel).
#
# systemd only runs the account and session phases for a service. The line
# that matters is pam_systemd: it registers a logind session on tty1, which
# gives the compositor its seat (DRM and input access) and creates
# XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (/run/user/<uid>), where the Wayland socket lives.
auth     required  pam_unix.so nullok
account  required  pam_unix.so
session  required  pam_unix.so
session  required  pam_systemd.so
